---
// The terms of Apassy Connect: the contract, the right of withdrawal, the consent
// to start at once, and the refund policy (implementation plan s7, owner-needed
// step 3). A DRAFT: the owner gives the facts in lib/legal.ts and has the text
// checked before it comes into force. Then remove `draft`, link it from the footer
// and from the Stripe settings. The prices come from lib/plans.ts.
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import OwnerFact from "../components/OwnerFact.astro";
import { FAMILY_EXTRA, FAMILY_INCLUDED_PEOPLE, PLANS, YEAR_MONTHS, eur } from "../lib/plans";
import { REPO } from "../lib/site";
const UPDATED = "2026-11-03";
---
<Legal
  draft
  title="Terms of Apassy Connect · apassy"
  description="The terms of Apassy Connect, the hosted service of the Apassy project."
  eyebrow="Terms"
  heading="Terms of Apassy Connect"
  updated={UPDATED}
>
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    These terms apply to Apassy Connect, the paid hosted service. The Apassy apps and everything that you host yourself
    are free and open source, and these terms do not apply to them.
  </Fragment>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Apassy Connect is sold by <OwnerFact name="legalName" what="legal name of the seller" />,
    <OwnerFact name="register" what="legal form and register entry" />,
    <OwnerFact name="address" what="postal address" />, VAT id <OwnerFact name="vatId" what="EU VAT id" />
    ("we"). Contact: <OwnerFact name="email" what="e-mail for contracts, withdrawal, and refunds" />. More in the
    <a href="/imprint">imprint</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are a <strong>consumer</strong> if you buy Connect mainly for purposes outside your trade, business, craft, or
    profession. Where the law of your country gives a sole trader the rights of a consumer for a contract that is not of
    a professional character for them, as Polish law does, those rights apply to you too. Rules marked "consumers" apply
    to those buyers. All other buyers are <strong>business customers</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What Connect is</h2>
  <p>Apassy Connect is optional. It gives the Apassy apps these hosted functions:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Reachability without Tailscale: a byte relay between your devices, with TLS end to end.</li>
    <li>An always-on sync home: a store for the encrypted copy of a vault.</li>
    <li>The hosted bouncer brain, only if you turn it on.</li>
    <li>Support.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Connect never receives your vault passphrase or a key that opens a credential, a vault, a question, or an answer.
    What Connect sees is in the <a href="/pricing#sees">pricing page</a> and the
    <a href="/privacy-connect">privacy policy</a>. Each function can also be hosted by you, at no cost, with the open
    source code at <a href={REPO}>GitHub</a> (Apache-2.0). That code comes with its own license, not with these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Account and devices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You make a Connect account in Apassy on your Mac. The account has no password. Each device has its own key, and you
      confirm each new device on a device that you already have.
    </li>
    <li>
      When you make the account, Apassy shows a recovery code once. Keep it safe. If you lose every device and the
      recovery code, we cannot give you access again. With the recovery code, you get access to the account, but the
      stored vault copies are deleted, because a new device cannot check them.
    </li>
    <li>
      You alone know your vault passphrase. We cannot read, reset, or recover it, or the contents of a vault. Keep
      your own copy of your vaults: Connect is a sync home, not your only backup.
    </li>
    <li>In a Connect Family, the organizer adds and removes members. In a Connect Team, the owner and the admins do.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Plans and prices</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">A month</th><th scope="col">A year</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {PLANS.map((plan) => (
        <tr><td>{plan.name}{plan.per && <>, {plan.per}</>}</td><td>{eur(plan.price.month)}</td><td>{eur(plan.price.year)}</td></tr>
      ))}
      <tr>
        <td>Connect Family, each person after {FAMILY_INCLUDED_PEOPLE}</td><td>{eur(FAMILY_EXTRA.month)}</td><td>{eur(FAMILY_EXTRA.year)}</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <ul>
    <li>Prices are in euro and include VAT. You pay the price that you see. A year costs {YEAR_MONTHS} months.</li>
    <li>You buy Connect in Apassy on your Mac, through a checkout page of our payment processor, Stripe.</li>
    <li>
      Your plan renews automatically at the end of each month or year, until you cancel it. We charge the payment method
      that you gave at the start of each period.
    </li>
    <li>
      When you add people to a Connect Family or seats to a Connect Team, we charge the share of the price for the rest
      of the current period. When you remove them, the next charge is lower; you get a credit for the rest of the period
      on your next invoice.
    </li>
    <li>
      We can change a price for the next period. We tell you at least 30 days before. If you do not agree, cancel before
      the new price applies.
    </li>
    <li>Stripe sends the receipts and the invoices by e-mail. Connect Team customers can add a VAT id at the checkout.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Cancel your plan</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      You can cancel at any time in Apassy on your Mac (Settings › Connect) or in the customer portal of Stripe. The plan
      then ends at the end of the period that you paid for.
    </li>
    <li>
      When a plan ends, or a payment fails and is not made good in 14 days, your account becomes read-only: you can still
      download your vault copies for 30 days, but not send new ones. 90 days after the end, we delete the stored vault
      copies. Apassy tells you before.
    </li>
    <li>
      When you delete your account in Apassy, we cancel the plan at once and delete your vault copies and devices. We
      keep the invoices for as long as tax law requires.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="withdrawal">6. Right of withdrawal (consumers)</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to withdraw from this contract within 14 days without giving any reason. The withdrawal period
    expires after 14 days from the day of the conclusion of the contract: the day of your first payment for a plan.
  </p>
  <p>
    To exercise the right of withdrawal, you must inform us (<OwnerFact name="legalName" what="legal name" />,
    <OwnerFact name="address" what="postal address" />, <OwnerFact name="email" what="e-mail" />) of your decision
    to withdraw from this contract by an unequivocal statement, for example an e-mail. You may use the model withdrawal
    form below, but it is not obligatory. To meet the withdrawal deadline, it is sufficient for you to send your
    communication before the withdrawal period has expired.
  </p>
  <h3>Effects of withdrawal</h3>
  <p>
    If you withdraw from this contract, we shall reimburse to you all payments received from you without undue delay and
    in any event not later than 14 days from the day on which we are informed about your decision to withdraw. We will
    carry out such reimbursement using the same means of payment as you used for the initial transaction, unless you have
    expressly agreed otherwise; in any event, you will not incur any fees as a result of such reimbursement.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you requested to begin the performance of the service during the withdrawal period, you shall pay us an amount
    which is in proportion to what has been provided until you have communicated to us your withdrawal from this
    contract, in comparison with the full coverage of the contract.
  </p>
  <h3 id="consent">Starting at once</h3>
  <p>
    Connect starts as soon as you pay, so the checkout asks for your request and your acknowledgement. The checkbox says:
  </p>
  <blockquote>
    I agree to the Terms of Apassy Connect. I ask that Connect starts at once. I know that if I withdraw within 14 days,
    I pay for the days that I used, and that I lose the right of withdrawal when the service is fully performed.
  </blockquote>
  <p>We confirm the contract, these terms, and your request by e-mail after the payment.</p>
  <h3>Model withdrawal form</h3>
  <blockquote>
    To <OwnerFact name="legalName" what="legal name" />, <OwnerFact name="address" what="postal address" />,
    <OwnerFact name="email" what="e-mail" />:<br />
    I hereby give notice that I withdraw from my contract for the provision of the following service: Apassy Connect
    (plan: …).<br />
    Ordered on: … / Account id (shown in Apassy › Settings › Connect): …<br />
    Name of consumer: … / Address of consumer: …<br />
    Signature of consumer (only if this form is notified on paper): …<br />
    Date: …
  </blockquote>

  <h2 id="refunds">7. Refunds</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A withdrawal within 14 days: as section 6 says.</li>
    <li>We refund in full a charge that we made by mistake, a double charge, and a charge after a cancellation that took effect.</li>
    <li>
      If we end Connect or your plan for a reason that is not your fault (section 9), we refund the part of the period that
      you paid for and cannot use.
    </li>
    <li>
      Apart from that, we do not refund the rest of a period after you cancel: the plan stays active until the end of the
      period. Your rights under the law (for example when the service does not conform to the contract) are not limited
      by this.
    </li>
    <li>Ask for a refund at <OwnerFact name="email" what="e-mail" />. The refund goes to the payment method of the charge.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>8. Fair use and our service</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Use Connect only for your own devices, your family, or your team, and only in a legal way. Do not use it to attack,
      overload, or probe Connect or other people, or to relay traffic that is not of Apassy.
    </li>
    <li>
      Each plan has limits for vault stores, devices, and data, shown in Apassy. We may slow down or stop traffic that
      harms the service or other customers, and we tell you why.
    </li>
    <li>
      We run Connect with care and fix faults as fast as we can, but we do not promise that it is always available.
      Without Connect, your Apassy apps keep working on your devices, and the free ways to sync and to approve stay open.
    </li>
    <li>We may change the functions of Connect. If a change takes away a main function of your plan, you can cancel and we refund the rest of the period.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>9. When we can end the contract</h2>
  <p>
    We can end the contract with 30 days of notice, or at once if you seriously break section 8. If we stop Connect as a
    whole, we tell you at least 60 days before, and you can download your vault copies until the end.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Liability</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      We are liable without limit for intent and gross negligence, for harm to life, body, or health, and where the law
      does not allow a limit.
    </li>
    <li>
      For other harm, we are liable to business customers only for foreseeable damage typical for this contract, and at
      most for the amount that the customer paid in the 12 months before the damage.
    </li>
    <li>For consumers, the rights under the law of the country where you live are not limited by these terms.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    We tell you about a change of these terms at least 30 days before it applies, in Apassy and by e-mail. If you do not
    agree, you can cancel before the change applies.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Law and disputes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      These terms are governed by <OwnerFact name="governingLaw" what="governing law" />. If you are a consumer, you also
      keep the protection of the mandatory law of the country where you live.
    </li>
    <li>
      Business customers: the courts of <OwnerFact name="courts" what="courts for business customers" /> decide disputes.
      Consumers can also go to the courts of the country where they live, and to a consumer body for an out-of-court
      settlement.
    </li>
    <li>Write to us first: <OwnerFact name="email" what="e-mail" />. We answer within 14 days.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These terms apply from <OwnerFact name="effectiveDate" what="date in force" />.</p>
</Legal>
